From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: bypass QDMA between ports without a
 switch

Offloaded flows go through a QDMA queue of their GMAC port.  The per-port
queues keep traffic to switch ports within their link speeds, but for a
port without a switch the queue only buffers, and it can hold megabytes.
When the port sends slower than the flows arrive, e.g. because its link
partner sends pause frames, the queue fills with the whole TCP window of
a flow and delays every other flow to that port behind it.  The ACKs of
the opposite direction wait behind it too, which can collapse a
bidirectional transfer.

Send a flow that comes in on a port without a switch and leaves on
another one from the PPE to the GDM directly, as MediaTek's HNAT does
unless HQoS is enabled.  When the port is paused, the frame engine then
pauses the sender, and the excess waits in the sender's own queue
instead of in QDMA.

Other flows keep their queues.  The frame engine would push back on the
port they come from, and a switch port or the WDMA carries the traffic of
many devices, which would all wait: a Wi-Fi station uploading to a slower
port would hold up everything received over Wi-Fi.

Based-on-patch-by: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/22213a321b6dafb2a5e01def97363420e6e938fd/25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-ppe-04-mtk_ppe-change-to-internal-QoS-mode.patch
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c
@@ -221,7 +221,7 @@ mtk_flow_get_dsa_port(struct net_device
 static int
 mtk_flow_set_output_device(struct mtk_eth *eth, struct mtk_foe_entry *foe,
 			   struct net_device *dev, const u8 *dest_mac,
-			   int *wed_index, u16 *wcid)
+			   int *wed_index, u16 *wcid, bool gmac_ingress)
 {
 	struct mtk_wdma_info info = {};
 	struct mtk_mac *mac;
@@ -271,13 +271,23 @@ mtk_flow_set_output_device(struct mtk_et
 			mtk_foe_entry_set_dsa(eth, foe, dsa_port);
 	}
 
-	if (dsa_port >= 0 && dsa_port < MTK_DSA_USER_PORT_MAX) {
-		mac = netdev_priv(dev);
-		queue = mac->dsa_queue_base + mac->dsa_port_rank[dsa_port];
-	} else {
-		queue = pse_port - 1;
+	/* A flow between two ports without a switch goes from the PPE to
+	 * the GDM directly: when the port is slower than the sender or
+	 * paused, a QDMA queue would hold a whole TCP window and delay every
+	 * other flow to the port behind it, while the frame engine pauses
+	 * the sender instead.  Other flows keep their QDMA queue: pushing
+	 * back on a switch port or on the WDMA would stall all the traffic
+	 * that comes in through it.
+	 */
+	if (dsa_port >= 0 || !gmac_ingress) {
+		if (dsa_port >= 0 && dsa_port < MTK_DSA_USER_PORT_MAX) {
+			mac = netdev_priv(dev);
+			queue = mac->dsa_queue_base + mac->dsa_port_rank[dsa_port];
+		} else {
+			queue = pse_port - 1;
+		}
+		mtk_foe_entry_set_queue(eth, foe, queue);
 	}
-	mtk_foe_entry_set_queue(eth, foe, queue);
 
 out:
 	mtk_foe_entry_set_pse_port(eth, foe, pse_port);
@@ -323,6 +333,7 @@ mtk_flow_offload_replace(struct mtk_eth
 	struct net_device *idev = NULL, *odev = NULL;
 	struct flow_action_entry *act;
 	struct mtk_flow_data data = {};
+	bool gmac_ingress = false;
 	struct mtk_foe_entry foe;
 	struct mtk_flow_entry *entry;
 	int offload_type = 0;
@@ -364,7 +375,7 @@ mtk_flow_offload_replace(struct mtk_eth
 			 * ppe[mac->ppe_idx]; the lookup misses and the
 			 * flow never binds in HW.
 			 */
-			mtk_flow_get_dsa_port(&idev, NULL);
+			gmac_ingress = mtk_flow_get_dsa_port(&idev, NULL) < 0;
 			if (mtk_flow_is_valid_idev(eth, idev)) {
 				struct mtk_mac *mac = netdev_priv(idev);
 
@@ -372,6 +383,8 @@ mtk_flow_offload_replace(struct mtk_eth
 					return -EINVAL;
 
 				ppe_index = mac->ppe_idx;
+			} else {
+				gmac_ingress = false;
 			}
 		}
 	} else {
@@ -548,7 +561,7 @@ mtk_flow_offload_replace(struct mtk_eth
 	}
 
 	err = mtk_flow_set_output_device(eth, &foe, odev, data.eth.h_dest,
-					 &wed_index, &wcid);
+					 &wed_index, &wcid, gmac_ingress);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
